WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.018 --> 00:00:02.929
- Any more passengers
for Llanfairpwllgwyngyll-

00:00:02.929 --> 00:00:06.211
gogerychwyrndrobwllllantysiliogogogoch?

00:00:06.211 --> 00:00:07.044
Anybody?

00:00:09.641 --> 00:00:11.988
Nope, anybody for Fan-Merc?

00:00:11.988 --> 00:00:14.137
- [Narrator] Plans-clull Llanfair

00:00:14.137 --> 00:00:16.581
- Llanfairpwllgwyngyllgogery-

00:00:16.581 --> 00:00:18.739
chwyrndrobwllllantysiliogogogoch.

00:00:18.739 --> 00:00:19.661
- [Narrator] Right.

00:00:19.661 --> 00:00:21.762
It's a small town in Northern Wales.

00:00:21.762 --> 00:00:25.482
Around 76% of the population
here speaks Welsh.

00:00:25.482 --> 00:00:27.402
It's also the longest town name in Europe

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:29.063
with 58 letters.

00:00:29.063 --> 00:00:32.583
There are literally four
Ls next to each other.

00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:33.813
Right there.

00:00:33.813 --> 00:00:35.554
What is with this name?

00:00:35.554 --> 00:00:37.983
- Llanfairpwllgwyngyllgogerychwyrndrobw-

00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:41.173
llllantysiliogogogoch
is not the original name

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:42.469
of the village.
(record scratching)

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:45.093
(sheep bleating)
- You've got to be kidding.

00:00:45.093 --> 00:00:49.291
- In the 1860s, the name was
contrived by the local cobbler,

00:00:49.291 --> 00:00:52.442
and it was meant to bring
in people and tourists.

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:54.253
- Alun, help us break this name down.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:58.431
- The name means places
within the village.

00:00:58.431 --> 00:01:00.810
You've got the Church Mary,

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.471
in the hollow of the white hazel,

00:01:03.471 --> 00:01:05.210
near to the rapid whirlpools,

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.242
at the Church of Tysilio,

00:01:07.242 --> 00:01:08.983
and the red caves.

00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:10.823
(laughing)

00:01:10.823 --> 00:01:13.423
- [Narrator] Okay, so, let's
say you wanna mail a letter.

00:01:13.423 --> 00:01:16.074
Do you have to write the whole
name, Postmaster Jim Evans?

00:01:16.074 --> 00:01:16.932
- You could.

00:01:16.932 --> 00:01:18.845
But you'd have to write very small.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.080
Or, you could use a shortened version,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.969
which is the first 20 letters.

00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:24.613
- [Narrator] If you play for
the local football league,

00:01:24.613 --> 00:01:26.002
does the name fit on your jersey,

00:01:26.002 --> 00:01:27.661
team manager Steve Smith?

00:01:27.661 --> 00:01:29.071
- It does, and it's the longest name

00:01:29.071 --> 00:01:31.181
of any football team in the world.

00:01:31.181 --> 00:01:32.690
And it just about fits.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:33.889
- Can you say it after a pint,

00:01:33.889 --> 00:01:35.141
pub owner Kevin Bryant?

00:01:35.141 --> 00:01:36.145
- I'm sure I can.

00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:37.438
Let's see.

00:01:37.438 --> 00:01:40.688
(bar patrons chatting)

00:01:42.558 --> 00:01:44.710
(belching) Llanfairpwllgwyngyllgogery-

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.529
chwyrndrobwllllantysiliogogogoch.

00:01:46.529 --> 00:01:48.747
- [Narrator] God, you did it.

00:01:48.747 --> 00:01:49.580
But,

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.406
can you put it in a song?

00:01:51.406 --> 00:01:53.023
♫ Llanfairpwllgwyngyllgogery

00:01:53.023 --> 00:01:54.992
♫ Chwyrndrobwllllantysilio

00:01:54.992 --> 00:01:56.875
♫ Gogogoch

00:01:56.875 --> 00:01:59.665
- [Narrator] Wow, apparently you can.

00:01:59.665 --> 00:02:01.494
Llanfair, Llanfair--

00:02:01.494 --> 00:02:03.542
- Llanfairpwllgwyngyllgogery-

00:02:03.542 --> 00:02:06.312
chwyrndrobwllllantysiliogogogoch.

00:02:06.312 --> 00:02:08.062
- [Narrator] It might
be the greatest PR stunt

00:02:08.062 --> 00:02:09.793
of the mid-1800s.

00:02:09.793 --> 00:02:11.563
I don't know, even of today.

00:02:11.563 --> 00:02:14.101
After all, we're here.

00:02:14.101 --> 00:02:16.743
Here in (clears throat)

00:02:16.743 --> 00:02:21.562
Llanfairpwllgwyngyllgogerychwyrndrobwllllantysiliogogogoch.

00:02:21.562 --> 00:02:23.514
I think that's pretty good.

00:02:23.514 --> 00:02:25.428
(upbeat music)

00:02:25.428 --> 00:02:28.345
(electronic music)

